{"title": "Sectional Mock #9 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>A container contains 240 kg of milk. From this container, 20 kg of milk was taken out and replaced with water. This process was repeated further two times. The (approx.) amount of milk left in the container is: </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;&#2344;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 240 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360; &#2325;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;&#2344;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; 20 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2354;&#2325;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2327;&#2361; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2337;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2379; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; &#2342;&#2379;&#2361;&#2352;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2325;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;&#2344;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2330;&#2366; &#2361;&#2369;&#2310; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; (&#2354;&#2327;&#2349;&#2327;) &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;: </p>", "options_en": ["192.86 l", "188.86 l", "184.86 l", "196. 86 l"], "options_hi": ["192.86 &#2354;&#2368;", "188.86 &#2354;&#2368;", "184.86 &#2354;&#2368;", "196. 86 &#2319;&#2354;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>a = Initial quantity </p><p>b = amount removed and replaced </p><p>n = number of times </p><p>Final Quantity = a * (1  -  b/a)<sup>n</sup></p><p>= 240 * (1  -  20/240)<sup>3</sup></p><p>= 240 * 11/12 * 11/12 * 11/12 </p><p>= 184.86 l</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>a = Initial quantity </p><p>b = amount removed and replaced </p><p>n = number of times </p><p>Final Quantity = a * (1  -  b/a)<sup>n</sup></p><p>= 240 * (1  -  20/240)<sup>3</sup></p><p>= 240 * 11/12 * 11/12 * 11/12 </p><p>= 184.86 l</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixture & Alligation"}, {"q_en": "<p>Workers A and B together can complete a task in 6 days, B and C together in 8 days, and A and C together in 12 days. In how many days can C alone complete the work?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2350;&#2332;&#2364;&#2342;&#2370;&#2352; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2325;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; 6 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, B &#2324;&#2352; C &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2325;&#2352; 8 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2324;&#2352; A &#2324;&#2352; C &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2325;&#2352; 12 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; C &#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; &#2313;&#2360; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["24", "32", "40", "48"], "options_hi": ["24", "32", "40", "48"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Sum of pair rates = 1/6 + 1/8 + 1/12 = (4 + 3 + 2)&#8201;&div;&#8201;24 = 9/24 = 3/8 per day</p><p>Sum of individual rates = (3/8) &div; 2 = 3/16 per day</p><p>A+B = 1/6 =&gt; C = (3/16)  -  (1/6) = (9/48  -  8/48) = 1/48 per day</p><p>C alone = 48 days</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Sum of pair rates = 1/6 + 1/8 + 1/12 = (4 + 3 + 2)&#8201;&div;&#8201;24 = 9/24 = 3/8 per day</p><p>Sum of individual rates = (3/8) &div; 2 = 3/16 per day</p><p>A+B = 1/6 =&gt; C = (3/16)  -  (1/6) = (9/48  -  8/48) = 1/48 per day</p><p>C alone = 48 days</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time & Work"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the smallest number which when increased by 15 is completely divisible by 11, 8, 12, 15 and 25.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2357;&#2361; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2379; 15 &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2338;&#2364;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; 11, 8, 12, 15 &#2324;&#2352; 25 &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2340;&#2307; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2379;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["6785", "6588", "7025", "6585"], "options_hi": ["6785", "6588", "7025", "6585"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Required number = (LCM of 11, 8, 12, 15, and 25)  -  15</p><p>Factor of 11 = 11</p><p>Factor of 8 = 2<sup>3</sup></p><p>Factor of 12 = 2<sup>2</sup> * 3</p><p>Factor of 15 = 3 * 5</p><p>Factor of 25 = 5<sup>2</sup></p><p>LCM = 11 * 2<sup>3</sup> * 3 * 5<sup>2 </sup>= 6600</p><p>Required number = 6600  -  15 = 6585</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Required number = (LCM of 11, 8, 12, 15, and 25)  -  15</p><p>Factor of 11 = 11</p><p>Factor of 8 = 2<sup>3</sup></p><p>Factor of 12 = 2<sup>2</sup> * 3</p><p>Factor of 15 = 3 * 5</p><p>Factor of 25 = 5<sup>2</sup></p><p>LCM = 11 * 2<sup>3</sup> * 3 * 5<sup>2 </sup>= 6600</p><p>Required number = 6600  -  15 = 6585</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "HCF & LCM"}, {"q_en": "<p>In what ratio must a shopkeeper mix two varieties of tea costing Rs.231 and Rs.253 per kg, respectively, to get a mixture of tea worth Rs.243 per kg?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; 243 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 231 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; 253 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2351; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2350;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["6: 1", "2: 1", "5: 6", "3: 4"], "options_hi": ["6: 1", "2: 1", "5: 6", "3: 4"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Using the Alligation method,</p><p>Required ratio = (253  -  243): (243  -  231)</p><p>= 10: 12</p><p>= 5: 6</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Using the Alligation method,</p><p>Required ratio = (253  -  243): (243  -  231)</p><p>= 10: 12</p><p>= 5: 6</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>A 4.2 m tall boy is 31&radic;3 m away from a shopping mall. The angle of elevation from his eye to the top of the shopping mall is 60&deg;. The height of the shopping mall is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>4.2 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2366; &#2358;&#2377;&#2346;&#2367;&#2306;&#2327; &#2350;&#2377;&#2354; &#2360;&#2375; 31&radic;3 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2305;&#2326; &#2360;&#2375; &#2358;&#2377;&#2346;&#2367;&#2306;&#2327; &#2350;&#2377;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2358;&#2368;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2366; &#2313;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; 60&deg; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2358;&#2377;&#2346;&#2367;&#2306;&#2327; &#2350;&#2377;&#2354; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["88.8 m", "97.2 m", "97.2&radic;3 m", "88.8&radic;3 m"], "options_hi": ["88.8 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "97.2 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "97.2&radic;3 &#2350;&#2368;", "88.8&radic;3 &#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=208 height=130 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27478/image002.png\"></p><p>AD = (AB + BD) = Height of shopping mall</p><p>BD = CE</p><p>CE = Height of boy</p><p>ED = Distance between boy and shopping mall</p><p>tan 60&deg; = AB/BC</p><p>&radic;3 = AB/31&radic;3</p><p>AB = 93 m</p><p>AD = 93 + 4.2 = 97.2 m</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=208 height=130 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27478/image002.png\"></p><p>AD = (AB + BD) = Height of shopping mall</p><p>BD = CE</p><p>CE = Height of boy</p><p>ED = Distance between boy and shopping mall</p><p>tan 60&deg; = AB/BC</p><p>&radic;3 = AB/31&radic;3</p><p>AB = 93 m</p><p>AD = 93 + 4.2 = 97.2 m</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Height & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>A cylinder has a radius of 7 cm and the area of its curved surface is 396 cm<sup>2</sup>. The volume of the cylinder is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 7 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 396 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; 2 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["1396 cm<sup>3</sup>", "1381 cm<sup>3</sup>", "1386 cm<sup>3</sup>", "1391 cm<sup>3</sup>"], "options_hi": ["1396 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup>", "1381 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup>", "1386 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup>", "1391 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup>"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Radius of cylinder = 7 cm</p><p>Curved surface area of cylinder = 396 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>2  X  (22/7)  X  7  X  h = 396</p><p>h = 396/44 </p><p>h = 9 cm </p><p>Volume of cylinder = &#960;r<sup>2</sup>h</p><p>= (22/7)  X  7<sup>2</sup>  X  9 </p><p>= 198  X  7</p><p>= 1386 cm<sup>3</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Radius of cylinder = 7 cm</p><p>Curved surface area of cylinder = 396 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>2  X  (22/7)  X  7  X  h = 396</p><p>h = 396/44 </p><p>h = 9 cm </p><p>Volume of cylinder = &#960;r<sup>2</sup>h</p><p>= (22/7)  X  7<sup>2</sup>  X  9 </p><p>= 198  X  7</p><p>= 1386 cm<sup>3</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>The ratio of the present age of P to that of Q is 2 : 5 respectively. 6 years hence, the ratio of the age of P to that of Q will become 4 : 7. What was the difference between their ages 4 years ago?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>P &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2324;&#2352; Q &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 2 : 5 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; 6 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342;, P &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2324;&#2352; Q &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 4 : 7 &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2327;&#2366;&#2404; 4 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["15 years", "9 years", "12 years", "7 years"], "options_hi": ["15 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;", "9 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;", "12 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;", "7 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let the present ages of P and Q be 2x and 5x respectively,</p><p>According to question,</p><p>(2x + 6)/(5x + 6) = 4/7</p><p>14x + 42 = 20x + 24</p><p>6x = 18</p><p>x = 3</p><p>Required difference = 5x  -  2x = 3x</p><p>=&gt; 3 * 3 = 9 years</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the present ages of P and Q be 2x and 5x respectively,</p><p>According to question,</p><p>(2x + 6)/(5x + 6) = 4/7</p><p>14x + 42 = 20x + 24</p><p>6x = 18</p><p>x = 3</p><p>Required difference = 5x  -  2x = 3x</p><p>=&gt; 3 * 3 = 9 years</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Average"}, {"q_en": "<p>In grade 9 of a school, 25 students opted for physics, 20 opted for biology, and 15 opted for Hindi. If the total of students in grade 9 was 50, all of these students opted for at least one of the three subjects mentioned here, and exactly four of these students opted for all these three subjects, what is the probability that a randomly selected student of grade 9 of this school would have opted for exactly one of these three subjects?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; 9 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 25 &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2344;&#2375; &#2349;&#2380;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2368;, 20 &#2344;&#2375; &#2332;&#2368;&#2357; &#2357;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2344; &#2324;&#2352; 15 &#2344;&#2375; &#2361;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2368; &#2357;&#2367;&#2359;&#2351; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; 9 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 50 &#2341;&#2368;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2311;&#2344; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2344;&#2375; &#2351;&#2361;&#2366;&#2305; &#2348;&#2340;&#2366;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2357;&#2367;&#2359;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2350; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2350; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2367;&#2359;&#2351; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366;, &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2344;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2336;&#2368;&#2325; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2344;&#2375; &#2311;&#2344; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2357;&#2367;&#2359;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2311;&#2360; &#2348;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2306;&#2349;&#2366;&#2357;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2325;&#2367; &#2311;&#2360; &#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; 9 &#2325;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2351;&#2366;&#2342;&#2371;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2367;&#2325; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344;&#2375; &#2327;&#2319; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2344;&#2375; &#2311;&#2344; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2357;&#2367;&#2359;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2336;&#2368;&#2325; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2367;&#2359;&#2351; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["0.65", "0.44", "0.88", "0.76"], "options_hi": ["0.65", "0.44", "0.88", "0.76"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Total students = 50 </p><p>Students who opted two or more subjects = 25 + 20 + 15  -  50  -  4 = 6</p><p>Students opted for exactly one subject = 50  -  6 = 44 </p><p>Hence, the required probability = 44/50 = 0.88 </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total students = 50 </p><p>Students who opted two or more subjects = 25 + 20 + 15  -  50  -  4 = 6</p><p>Students opted for exactly one subject = 50  -  6 = 44 </p><p>Hence, the required probability = 44/50 = 0.88 </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Probability"}, {"q_en": "<p>If m + 5 = sec<sup>2</sup> A cosec<sup>2</sup> A(1  -  cos<sup>2</sup> A)(1  -  sin<sup>2</sup>A) + 5, then find the value of m : </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; m + 5 = sec<sup>2</sup> A cosec<sup>2</sup> A(1 - cos<sup>2</sup> A)(1 - sin<sup>2</sup>A) + 5, &#2340;&#2379; m &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;:</p>", "options_en": ["10", "0", "1", "5"], "options_hi": ["10", "0", "1", "5"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>sec&#178;A = 1/cos&#178;A</p><p>cosec&#178;A = 1/sin&#178;A</p><p>1 - cos&#178;A = sin&#178;A</p><p>1 - sin&#178;A = cos&#178;A</p><p>m + 5 = sec&#178;A  X  cosec&#178;A  X  sin&#178;A  X  cos&#178;A + 5</p><p>Substitute sec&#178;A = 1/cos&#178;A and cosec&#178;A = 1/sin&#178;A:</p><p>m + 5 = (1/cos&#178;A)  X  (1/sin&#178;A)  X  sin&#178;A  X  cos&#178;A + 5</p><p>m + 5 = (1  X  cos&#178;A  X  sin&#178;A) / (cos&#178;A  X  sin&#178;A) + 5</p><p>m + 5 = 1 + 5</p><p>m + 5 = 6</p><p>m = 6  -  5 = 1</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>sec&#178;A = 1/cos&#178;A</p><p>cosec&#178;A = 1/sin&#178;A</p><p>1 - cos&#178;A = sin&#178;A</p><p>1 - sin&#178;A = cos&#178;A</p><p>m + 5 = sec&#178;A  X  cosec&#178;A  X  sin&#178;A  X  cos&#178;A + 5</p><p>Substitute sec&#178;A = 1/cos&#178;A and cosec&#178;A = 1/sin&#178;A:</p><p>m + 5 = (1/cos&#178;A)  X  (1/sin&#178;A)  X  sin&#178;A  X  cos&#178;A + 5</p><p>m + 5 = (1  X  cos&#178;A  X  sin&#178;A) / (cos&#178;A  X  sin&#178;A) + 5</p><p>m + 5 = 1 + 5</p><p>m + 5 = 6</p><p>m = 6  -  5 = 1</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>The following pie chart shows the study time of different subjects of a student in a day. Study the pie chart and answer the question. </p><p><b><img width=520 height=336 id=\"Chart 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27004/image024.png\"></b></p><p>If the student studied English for 3 hours, then he studied Mathematics for: </p>", "q_hi": "&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344; &#2346;&#2366;&#2312; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2335; &#2319;&#2325; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2357;&#2367;&#2359;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2346;&#2366;&#2312; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2335; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2358;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2342;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p><p><b><img width=520 height=336 id=\"Chart 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27004/image024.png\"></b></p><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2344;&#2375; 3 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2332;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2327;&#2339;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;:", "options_en": ["2 hours", "1 hour", "7 hours", "5 hours"], "options_hi": ["2 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "1 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "7 &#2327;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "5 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>According to question, </p><p>3 = (15  X  Total study time) &div; 100</p><p>=&gt; Total study time = (3  X  100) &div; 15 = 20 hours</p><p>Actual study time for Mathematics = (35  X  20) &div; 100 = 7 hours</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>According to question, </p><p>3 = (15  X  Total study time) &div; 100</p><p>=&gt; Total study time = (3  X  100) &div; 15 = 20 hours</p><p>Actual study time for Mathematics = (35  X  20) &div; 100 = 7 hours</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>If the perimeter of the square is 64 cm. What is the area of a circle whose radius is half of the side of the square?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; 64 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;, &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2343;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["64&pi; cm<sup>2</sup>", "144&pi; cm<sup>2</sup>", "62&pi; cm<sup>2</sup>", "36&pi; cm<sup>2</sup>"], "options_hi": ["64&pi; cm<sup>2</sup>", "144&pi; cm<sup>2</sup>", "62&pi; cm<sup>2</sup>", "36&pi; cm<sup>2</sup>"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Perimeter of square A = 64 cm</p><p>Side of square A = P/4 = 16 cm</p><p>Radius of the circle is = &pi;r<sup>2</sup></p><p>Area of circle = &pi; x 8 x 8 = 64&pi; cm<sup>2</sup></p><p></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Perimeter of square A = 64 cm</p><p>Side of square A = P/4 = 16 cm</p><p>Radius of the circle is = &pi;r<sup>2</sup></p><p>Area of circle = &pi; x 8 x 8 = 64&pi; cm<sup>2</sup></p><p></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Pipe P, Q and R can fill a tank in 15 minutes, 20 minutes and 40 minutes respectively. What is the time taken to fill the tank when all three pipes are opened together?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; P, Q &#2324;&#2352; R &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 15 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;, 20 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2324;&#2352; 40 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2332;&#2348; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2326;&#2379;&#2354; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2349;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2354;&#2327;&#2375;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["7 (1/12) minutes", "8 (2/17) minutes", "9 (1/17) minutes", "7 (1/17) minutes"], "options_hi": ["7 (1/12) &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "8 (2/17) &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "9 (1/17) &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "7 (1/17) &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Capacity of tank = LCM of 15, 20 and 40 = 120 unit</p><p>Efficiency of pipe P = 120/15 = 8 unit</p><p>Efficiency of pipe Q = 120/20 = 6 unit</p><p>Efficiency of pipe R = 120/40 = 3 unit</p><p>Time taken to fill tank when all pipes are opened together = 120/(8 + 6 + 3)</p><p>= 120/17 or 7 (1/17) minutes</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Capacity of tank = LCM of 15, 20 and 40 = 120 unit</p><p>Efficiency of pipe P = 120/15 = 8 unit</p><p>Efficiency of pipe Q = 120/20 = 6 unit</p><p>Efficiency of pipe R = 120/40 = 3 unit</p><p>Time taken to fill tank when all pipes are opened together = 120/(8 + 6 + 3)</p><p>= 120/17 or 7 (1/17) minutes</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Pipes & Cisterns"}, {"q_en": "<p>A boat covers 24 km upstream and 36 km downstream in 10 hours, and 36 km upstream and 24 km downstream in 12 hours. The speed of the current is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; 10 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 24 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; &#2324;&#2352; 36 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; 12 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 36 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; &#2324;&#2352; 24 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; &#2330;&#2354;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["26/9 km/h", "33/13 km/h", "25/8 km/h", "24/7 km/h"], "options_hi": ["26/9 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "33/13 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "25/8 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "24/7 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let boat's speed = b km/h</p><p>Current's speed = s km/h</p><p>Let 1/(b  -  s) = u, 1/(b + s) = v</p><p>ATQ  - </p><p>24/(b - s) + 36/(b + s) = 10 </p><p>12u + 18v = 5 -----(1)</p><p>36/(b - s) + 24/(b + s) = 12 </p><p>12u + 8v = 4 -----(2)</p><p>eqn(1)  -  eqn(2):</p><p>10v = 1</p><p>v = 1/10</p><p>b + s = 10 ----(3)</p><p>12u + 8*1/10 = 4</p><p>12u = 4  -  4/5 = 16/5</p><p>u = 4/15</p><p>b  -  s = 15/4 ----(4)</p><p>Eqn(3)  -  eqn(4):</p><p>(b + s)  -  (b  -  s) = 10  -  15/4</p><p>2s = 25/4</p><p>s = 25/8</p><p>Current's speed = 25/8 km/h</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let boat's speed = b km/h</p><p>Current's speed = s km/h</p><p>Let 1/(b  -  s) = u, 1/(b + s) = v</p><p>ATQ  - </p><p>24/(b - s) + 36/(b + s) = 10 </p><p>12u + 18v = 5 -----(1)</p><p>36/(b - s) + 24/(b + s) = 12 </p><p>12u + 8v = 4 -----(2)</p><p>eqn(1)  -  eqn(2):</p><p>10v = 1</p><p>v = 1/10</p><p>b + s = 10 ----(3)</p><p>12u + 8*1/10 = 4</p><p>12u = 4  -  4/5 = 16/5</p><p>u = 4/15</p><p>b  -  s = 15/4 ----(4)</p><p>Eqn(3)  -  eqn(4):</p><p>(b + s)  -  (b  -  s) = 10  -  15/4</p><p>2s = 25/4</p><p>s = 25/8</p><p>Current's speed = 25/8 km/h</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>If 2a + 4b + 5c = 0, then what is the value of (8a<sup>3</sup> + 64b<sup>3</sup> + 125c<sup>3</sup>) ?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 2a + 4b + 5c = 0, &#2340;&#2379; (8a<sup>3</sup> + 64b<sup>3</sup> + 125c<sup>3</sup>) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["90abc", "100abc", "120abc", "125abc"], "options_hi": ["90&#2319;&#2348;&#2368;&#2360;&#2368;", "100&#2319;&#2348;&#2368;&#2360;&#2368;", "120&#2319;&#2348;&#2368;&#2360;&#2368;", "125&#2319;&#2348;&#2368;&#2360;&#2368;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>We use the identity for the sum of cubes: a<sup>3</sup> + b<sup>3</sup> + c<sup>3</sup> - 3abc</p><p>=&gt; (a + b + c)(a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup> - ab - bc - ca)</p><p><b>Formula Used:</b></p><p>8a<sup>3</sup> + 64b<sup>3</sup> + 125c<sup>3</sup>  -  3(2a)(4b)(5c) = (2a + 4b + 5c)[(2a)<sup>2</sup> + (4b)<sup>2</sup> + (5c)<sup>2</sup>  -  (2a)(4b) - (4b)(5c) - (5c)(2a)]</p><p><b>Calculation:</b></p><p>We have,</p><p>=&gt; 2a + 4b + 5c = 0</p><p>Using the formula for the sum of cubes, we get:</p><p>=&gt; 8a<sup>3</sup> + 64b<sup>3</sup> + 125c<sup>3</sup>  -  120abc = (2a + 4b + 5c)(4a<sup>2</sup> + 16b<sup>2</sup> + 25c<sup>2</sup> - 8ab - 20bc - 10ca)</p><p>=&gt; 8a<sup>3</sup> + 64b<sup>3</sup> + 125c<sup>3</sup>  -  120abc = 0</p><p>=&gt; 8a<sup>3</sup> + 64b<sup>3</sup> + 125c<sup>3</sup> = 120abc</p><p><b>The value of 8a<sup>3</sup> + 64b<sup>3</sup> + 125c<sup>3</sup> is 120abc.</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>We use the identity for the sum of cubes: a<sup>3</sup> + b<sup>3</sup> + c<sup>3</sup> - 3abc</p><p>=&gt; (a + b + c)(a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup> - ab - bc - ca)</p><p><b>Formula Used:</b></p><p>8a<sup>3</sup> + 64b<sup>3</sup> + 125c<sup>3</sup>  -  3(2a)(4b)(5c) = (2a + 4b + 5c)[(2a)<sup>2</sup> + (4b)<sup>2</sup> + (5c)<sup>2</sup>  -  (2a)(4b) - (4b)(5c) - (5c)(2a)]</p><p><b>Calculation:</b></p><p>We have,</p><p>=&gt; 2a + 4b + 5c = 0</p><p>Using the formula for the sum of cubes, we get:</p><p>=&gt; 8a<sup>3</sup> + 64b<sup>3</sup> + 125c<sup>3</sup>  -  120abc = (2a + 4b + 5c)(4a<sup>2</sup> + 16b<sup>2</sup> + 25c<sup>2</sup> - 8ab - 20bc - 10ca)</p><p>=&gt; 8a<sup>3</sup> + 64b<sup>3</sup> + 125c<sup>3</sup>  -  120abc = 0</p><p>=&gt; 8a<sup>3</sup> + 64b<sup>3</sup> + 125c<sup>3</sup> = 120abc</p><p><b>The value of 8a<sup>3</sup> + 64b<sup>3</sup> + 125c<sup>3</sup> is 120abc.</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the value of N, if N = 5 + 55 + 555 + .... + 55555555.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; N = 5 + 55 + 555 + .... + 55555555 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; N &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["61728390", "61548770", "61296130", "61997230"], "options_hi": ["61728390", "61548770", "61296130", "61997230"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>N = 5 + 55 + 555 + .... + 55555555</p><p>N = 5 * (1 + 11 + 111 + .... + 11111111)</p><p>N = 5 * (12345678)</p><p><b>N = 61728390</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>N = 5 + 55 + 555 + .... + 55555555</p><p>N = 5 * (1 + 11 + 111 + .... + 11111111)</p><p>N = 5 * (12345678)</p><p><b>N = 61728390</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>An article is available for Rs.2500 cash for Rs.520 cash down payments followed by 4 equal monthly Instalments. if the rate of interest is 25% per annum, calculate the monthly Instalment? </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; 2500 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2344;&#2325;&#2342; &#2324;&#2352; 520 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2344;&#2325;&#2342; &#2337;&#2366;&#2313;&#2344; &#2346;&#2375;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306;&#2335; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; 4 &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2350;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2325; &#2325;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2352; &#2313;&#2346;&#2354;&#2348;&#2381;&#2343; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; 25% &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2350;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2325; &#2325;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2339;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs.520", "Rs.481", "Rs.576", "Rs.500"], "options_hi": ["520 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "481 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "576 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "500 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p> Cash price = 2500</p><p>Downpayment = 520 </p><p>Remaining amount = 2500 &#8211; 520 = 1980 </p><p>Rate = 25% </p><p>Let each Instalment be Rs x, then,</p><p> Amt. paid = 4 <i>x</i></p><p> Interest paid = 4 <i>x</i> &#8211; 1980</p><p>Considering time to be 1 month, principal will be, </p><p> (1980) + (1980 &#8211; <i>x</i> ) + (1980 &#8211; 2 <i>x</i> ) + (1980 &#8211; 3 <i>x</i> )</p><p>Now, P = 1980 &#215; 4 &#8211; 6x</p><p>= 7920 &#8211; 6x </p><p>R = 25% , T = 1 month, Int. = 4x &#8211; 1980 </p><p> <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/285337d3e32c591f6981820b217f730b.png\" /> </p>", "solution_hi": "<p> Cash price = 2500</p><p>Downpayment = 520 </p><p>Remaining amount = 2500 &#8211; 520 = 1980 </p><p>Rate = 25% </p><p>Let each Instalment be Rs x, then,</p><p> Amt. paid = 4 <i>x</i></p><p> Interest paid = 4 <i>x</i> &#8211; 1980</p><p>Considering time to be 1 month, principal will be, </p><p> (1980) + (1980 &#8211; <i>x</i> ) + (1980 &#8211; 2 <i>x</i> ) + (1980 &#8211; 3 <i>x</i> )</p><p>Now, P = 1980 &#215; 4 &#8211; 6x</p><p>= 7920 &#8211; 6x </p><p>R = 25% , T = 1 month, Int. = 4x &#8211; 1980 </p><p> <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/285337d3e32c591f6981820b217f730b.png\" /> </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;If a =&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">&radic;3 + &radic;2", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; a = &nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">&radic;3 + &radic;2", "options_en": ["960", "970", "980", "990"], "options_hi": ["960", "970", "980", "990"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/7bda43936777487587fa872a052e9ca5.png\"/></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/7bda43936777487587fa872a052e9ca5.png\"/></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>What is the mean of the median and the mode of the data?</p><p>29, 30, 24, 25, 29, 26, 27, 25, 24, 23, 28, 29, 27</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2310;&#2306;&#2325;&#2337;&#2364;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2361;&#2369;&#2354;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p>29, 30, 24, 25, 29, 26, 27, 25, 24, 23, 28, 29, 27</p>", "options_en": ["28", "27", "29", "30"], "options_hi": ["28", "27", "29", "30"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Data in ascending order: 23, 24, 24, 25, 25, 26, 27, 27, 28, 29, 29, 29, 30</p><p>Median = 7<sup>th</sup> term = 27</p><p>Mode = Higher frequency term = 29</p><p>Required mean = (27 + 29)/2 = 56/2 = 28</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Data in ascending order: 23, 24, 24, 25, 25, 26, 27, 27, 28, 29, 29, 29, 30</p><p>Median = 7<sup>th</sup> term = 27</p><p>Mode = Higher frequency term = 29</p><p>Required mean = (27 + 29)/2 = 56/2 = 28</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Statistics"}, {"q_en": "<p>Rohan invested Rs. 12000 for 2 years and Brijendra invested Rs.12000 in the first year and invested additional Rs.8000 for the second year. Brijendra's share fraction in profit is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2352;&#2379;&#2361;&#2344; &#2344;&#2375; 2 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; 12000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2371;&#2332;&#2375;&#2344;&#2381;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; &#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 12000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; 8000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2340;&#2367;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2371;&#2332;&#2375;&#2344;&#2381;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["3/4", "3/7", "4/7", "4/5"], "options_hi": ["3/4", "3/7", "4/7", "4/5"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Profits are proportional to the value of investment made.</p><p>Ratio of investments = <img width=265 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20245/image015.png\"></p><p>Brijendra's share fraction in profit = <img width=64 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20245/image016.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Profits are proportional to the value of investment made.</p><p>Ratio of investments = <img width=265 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20245/image015.png\"></p><p>Brijendra's share fraction in profit = <img width=64 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20245/image016.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>Simplify: [25 &#8722;48 &div; 6 + 12  X  2] + 78  -  [5 + 3 of (25  -  2  X  10)]</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2352;&#2354;&#2368;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;: [25 &#8722;48 &div; 6 + 12 X 2] + 78 - [5 + 3 of (25 - 2 X 10)]</p>", "options_en": ["98", "90", "99", "89"], "options_hi": ["98", "90", "99", "89"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>We have the equation as:-</p><p>[25 &#8722;48 &div; 6 + 12  X  2] + 78  -  [5 + 3 of (25  -  2  X  10)]</p><p>= [25 &#8722;8 + 24] + 78  -  [5 + 3 of (5)]</p><p>= [41] + 78  -  [20]</p><p>= 119  -  20 </p><p>= 99</p><p>Option (c) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>We have the equation as:-</p><p>[25 &#8722;48 &div; 6 + 12  X  2] + 78  -  [5 + 3 of (25  -  2  X  10)]</p><p>= [25 &#8722;8 + 24] + 78  -  [5 + 3 of (5)]</p><p>= [41] + 78  -  [20]</p><p>= 119  -  20 </p><p>= 99</p><p>Option (c) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p>A person can hit a target 5 times out of 12 shorts. If he fires 14 shorts, what is the probability that he will hit the target twice?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; 12 &#2358;&#2377;&#2335; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 5 &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2354;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2354;&#2327;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2361; 14 &#2358;&#2377;&#2335; &#2342;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2306;&#2349;&#2366;&#2357;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2325;&#2367; &#2357;&#2361; &#2354;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2342;&#2379; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2319;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["[2275 * 7<sup>12</sup>]/12<sup>14</sup>", "[2275 * 7<sup>2</sup>]/12<sup>12</sup>", "[2275 * 7<sup>6</sup>]/12<sup>8</sup>", "[2275 * 7<sup>5</sup>]/12<sup>11</sup>"], "options_hi": ["[2275 * 7<sup>12</sup>]/12<sup>14</sup>", "[2275 * 7<sup>2</sup>]/12<sup>12</sup>", "[2275 * 7<sup>6</sup>]/12<sup>8</sup>", "[2275 * 7<sup>5</sup>]/12<sup>11</sup>"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Probability of hit = 5/12</p><p>Probability of miss = 7/12</p><p>Hence, the required probability = <sup>14</sup>C<sub>2 </sub>(5/12 * 5/12)<sup>2</sup> * [7/12]<sup>12</sup></p><p>= [2275 * 7<sup>12</sup>]/12<sup>14</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Probability of hit = 5/12</p><p>Probability of miss = 7/12</p><p>Hence, the required probability = <sup>14</sup>C<sub>2 </sub>(5/12 * 5/12)<sup>2</sup> * [7/12]<sup>12</sup></p><p>= [2275 * 7<sup>12</sup>]/12<sup>14</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Probability"}, {"q_en": "<p>Pipe A fills a tank in 12 h and pipe B in 15 h. Both are opened, and after 4 h pipe C, which empties a full tank in 20 h, is also opened. How long from the start will the tank be full?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; A &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; 12 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; B 15 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2326;&#2379;&#2354; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2324;&#2352; 4 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; C, &#2332;&#2379; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; 20 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2326;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2325;&#2379; &#2349;&#2368; &#2326;&#2379;&#2354; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2349;&#2352; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2327;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["7 h", "8 h", "9 h", "10 h"], "options_hi": ["7 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "8 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "9 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "10 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Rate of (A+B) = 1/12+1/15 = 3/20</p><p>Work in 4 h = 4 X 3/20 = 3/5</p><p>Rate of C = &#8722;1/20</p><p>=&gt; new net rate = 3/20 &#8722;1/20 = 1/10</p><p>Remaining work = 2/5</p><p>Time to finish = (2/5)/(1/10) = 4 h</p><p>Total time = 4 + 4 = 8 h</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Rate of (A+B) = 1/12+1/15 = 3/20</p><p>Work in 4 h = 4 X 3/20 = 3/5</p><p>Rate of C = &#8722;1/20</p><p>=&gt; new net rate = 3/20 &#8722;1/20 = 1/10</p><p>Remaining work = 2/5</p><p>Time to finish = (2/5)/(1/10) = 4 h</p><p>Total time = 4 + 4 = 8 h</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Pipes & Cisterns"}, {"q_en": "<p>The marks obtained by 15 students out of a maximum of 25 in a test are given as 13, 11, 16, 15, 18, 12, 13, 14, 10, 22, 15, 21, 20, 17 and 24. Find the product of the modes of this set of data.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 15 &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325;&#2340;&#2350; 25 &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; 13, 11, 16, 15, 18, 12, 13, 14, 10, 22, 15, 21, 20, 17 &#2324;&#2352; 24 &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2310;&#2305;&#2325;&#2396;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2311;&#2360; &#2360;&#2350;&#2370;&#2361; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2361;&#2369;&#2354;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2344;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["182", "192", "195", "210"], "options_hi": ["182", "192", "195", "210"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><b>Mode:</b> The mode is the value that appears most frequently in a data set.</p><p><b>Data:</b> 13, 11, 16, 15, 18, 12, 13, 14, 10, 22, 15, 21,20, 17 and 24</p><p>In the above data sets, 13 and 15 appears twice which means 13 and 15 will be the mode of the given data sets.</p><p>Product of modes = 13 * 15</p><p>= 195</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><b>Mode:</b> The mode is the value that appears most frequently in a data set.</p><p><b>Data:</b> 13, 11, 16, 15, 18, 12, 13, 14, 10, 22, 15, 21,20, 17 and 24</p><p>In the above data sets, 13 and 15 appears twice which means 13 and 15 will be the mode of the given data sets.</p><p>Product of modes = 13 * 15</p><p>= 195</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Statistics"}, {"q_en": "<p>X is inversely proportional to Y and inversely proportional to square of Z. When Y = 10 and Z = 4, then X = 12. What will be the value of Z when X = 16, and Y = 3?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>X, Y &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; Z &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; Y = 10 &#2324;&#2352; Z = 4 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; X = 12 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; X = 16 &#2324;&#2352; Y = 3 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; Z &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["&radic;10", "2&radic;10", "2&radic;5", "&radic;5"], "options_hi": ["&radic;10", "2&radic;10", "2&radic;5", "&radic;5"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=60 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22970/image001.png\"></p><p><img width=59 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22970/image002.png\"></p><p><img width=84 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22970/image003.png\"></p><p><img width=65 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22970/image004.png\"></p><p><img width=39 height=19 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22970/image005.png\"></p><p><img width=77 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22970/image006.png\"></p><p><img width=56 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22970/image007.png\"></p><p><img width=65 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22970/image008.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=60 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22970/image001.png\"></p><p><img width=59 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22970/image002.png\"></p><p><img width=84 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22970/image003.png\"></p><p><img width=65 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22970/image004.png\"></p><p><img width=39 height=19 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22970/image005.png\"></p><p><img width=77 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22970/image006.png\"></p><p><img width=56 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22970/image007.png\"></p><p><img width=65 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22970/image008.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>If tan&#952; = 11/60, then the value of 2tanY*3cosecY  -  4secY is ________.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; tan&#952; = 11/60, &#2340;&#2379; 2tanY*3cosecY - 4secY &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; ________ &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["61/60", "150/61", "121/30", "61/30"], "options_hi": ["61/60", "150/61", "121/30", "61/30"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>tan&#952; = 11/60</p><p>Perpendicular = 11, Base = 60</p><p>Hypotenuse = &radic;(11<sup>2</sup> + 60<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>= &radic;(121 + 3600)</p><p>= 61</p><p>=&gt; 2tanY*3cosecY  -  4secY</p><p>= 6 * 11/60 * 61/11  -  4* 61/60</p><p>= 61/10  -  61/15</p><p>= 61/30</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>tan&#952; = 11/60</p><p>Perpendicular = 11, Base = 60</p><p>Hypotenuse = &radic;(11<sup>2</sup> + 60<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>= &radic;(121 + 3600)</p><p>= 61</p><p>=&gt; 2tanY*3cosecY  -  4secY</p><p>= 6 * 11/60 * 61/11  -  4* 61/60</p><p>= 61/10  -  61/15</p><p>= 61/30</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}]}